          "guid": "ms2y8xqw48qc36kl",
          "message": {
            "text": "The env-var-only gate was verified unreachable in a browser before this module was written — the attached artifact is the bundled output and the run.\n\nTwo things had to be true for the ticket's claim to hold, and both were checked rather than assumed. First, esbuild's --define:process.env.KERFDEVWARNNARROWSET='\"1\"' does NOT reach the read: the bundle still contains const proc = globalThis.process; return proc?.env?.KERFDEVWARNNARROWSET === \"1\", because the value passes through a local binding and no process.env.X token survives to substitute. Second, evaluating that bundle in a realm with no process (vm context, typeof process === 'undefined') emitted zero warnings for a narrow set the consumer had explicitly opted into.\n\nSo devFlag() keeps the globalThis.process indirection — removing it would reintroduce the production-browser-infers-DEVELOPMENT bug — and adds the in-memory map as the switch that is reachable everywhere. tests/unit/dev-warn-config.internal.test.ts pins both halves, including a test that deletes globalThis.process and asserts the env-var path stays dead while the API path works.\n",
            "markdown": "The env-var-only gate was verified unreachable in a browser before this module was written — the attached artifact is the bundled output and the run.\n\nTwo things had to be true for the ticket's claim to hold, and both were checked rather than assumed. First, esbuild's `--define:process.env.KERF_DEV_WARN_NARROW_SET='\"1\"'` does NOT reach the read: the bundle still contains `const proc = globalThis.process; return proc?.env?.KERF_DEV_WARN_NARROW_SET === \"1\"`, because the value passes through a local binding and no `process.env.X` token survives to substitute. Second, evaluating that bundle in a realm with no `process` (`vm` context, `typeof process === 'undefined'`) emitted **zero** warnings for a narrow set the consumer had explicitly opted into.\n\nSo `devFlag()` keeps the `globalThis.process` indirection — removing it would reintroduce the production-browser-infers-DEVELOPMENT bug — and adds the in-memory map as the switch that is reachable everywhere. `tests/unit/dev-warn-config.internal.test.ts` pins both halves, including a test that deletes `globalThis.process` and asserts the env-var path stays dead while the API path works.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/dev-warn-config.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 95,
                  "endLine": 108,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  }\n}\n\n/**\n * The value of one diagnostic switch, or `undefined` when it is off.\n * Every warner's opt-in check goes through here.\n */\nexport function devFlag(envName: string): string | undefined {\n  const override = overrides.get(envName);\n  if (override !== undefined) return override === false ? undefined : override;\n  const proc = (globalThis as { process?: { env?: Record<string, string | undefined> } }).process;\n  return proc?.env?.[envName];\n}\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
